I think we should rather write this as:

```
pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, e.entity_type);
pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, e.entity_instance_num);
pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, e.entity_container_id);
rc = pldm_msgbuf_destroy_consumed(buf);
if (rc) {
    return;
}
```

Let the `pldm_msgbuf_destroy_consumed()` do the error handling for you to make it less tedious.

However, no doubt we should have a `static int decode_pldm_entity(const void *buf, size_t len, sturct pldm_entity *e)` to do this for us 😊
